{
  "title": "Brief Manners & Talqeen to Be Recited near the Dying",
  "data": "One whom death approaches should be laid facing the qiblah with the soles of the feet towards it. In his presence, someone should recite [Surah Ya-Sin](A40) and [Surah al-Saffat](A41), and prompt the dying person to say the two testimonies of Islam, to affirm the Holy Imams by name, and to say the following words of relief (Kalimat al-Faraj):\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ الْحَلِيْمُ الْكَرِيْمُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ الْعَلِىُّ الْعَظِيْمُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHUL HALEEMUL KAREEMU LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHUL A'LIYYUL A'ZEEM\nThere is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great.\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ السَّمٰوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبِّ الْاَرَضِيْنَ السَّبْعِ وَمَا فِيْهِنَّ وَمَا بَيْنَهُنَّ وَمَا تَحْتَهُنَّ وَرَبِّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI RABBIS SAMAAWAATIS SAB'I WA RABBIL ARADEENAS SAB'I WA MAA FEEHINNA WA MAA BAYNAHUNNA WA MAA TAHTAHUNNA WA RABBIL A'RSHIL A'ZEEM\nGlory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the seven earths, of what is in them, what is between them and what is beneath them, and Lord of the Mighty Throne.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَالصَّلَوٰةُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEENA WAS SALAATU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAYYIBEEN\nAnd all praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds, and blessings be upon Muhammad and his good Household.\nNo one in a state of ritual impurity, and no menstruating woman, should be present with the dying person."
}
